{"title":"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three students took a 3-question quiz. Their teacher recorded their answers in a chart:\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/f/16fb045fb6410689d5b795993bf247c93af9ee0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{array}{|l|c|c|c|} \\hline &amp; \\textbf{Question \\#1} &amp; \\textbf{Question \\#2} &amp; \\textbf{Question \\#3} \\\\ \\hline \\textbf{Student A} &amp; 15 &amp; 36 &amp; 24 \\\\ \\hline \\textbf{Student B} &amp; 20 &amp; 38 &amp; 24 \\\\ \\hline \\textbf{Student C} &amp; 15 &amp; 54 &amp; 24 \\\\ \\hline \\end{array}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -38px\" width=\"472\" height=\"85\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Each student answered exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> questions correctly. What is the sum of the correct answers to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> questions?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/9/679888bf57d78b4e00563a78ef07b25038012b9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 75 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 77 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 80 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 82 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 93$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> must be the correct answer to problem 3 because the students had different answers for problems 1 and 2 but not 3.\n</p><p>However, everyone had a different answer for problem 2 while 2 people had the same answer for problem 1, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> must be the correct answer to problem 1.\n</p><p>This means that student B got problem 1 wrong but got problem 2 and 3 right, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c5e2e4c4950cff11894abd202aa2949e21819c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$38$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> must be the correct answer to problem 2.\n</p><p>Thus, the correct answers sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/b/0ab75fdd9405c104a1510d55a40d64f43b8d7250.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 + 24 + 38 = 39 + 38 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 77}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"272\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal (page does not exist)\">2025 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title